 "diagnosis": "The postcondition upper bound is off by one. It uses '(j + a[j]) + 1' (i.e., k <= j + a[j]) but the loop invariant only proves a[k] != 0 for k < j + a[j]. At k = j + a[j], the invariant a[j] - (i-j) <= a[i] yields only 0 <= a[j+a[j]], not > 0. The fix is to change the postcondition bound from '(j + a[j]) + 1' to 'j + a[j]', making it 'j <= k < j + a[j]'. The caller FindZero only needs this weaker bound since it sets index := index + a[index] and the new invariant only requires non-zero for k < new_index."}

